.TH SWAYDESK-DESKTOP-CONFIG 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.2.1" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-desktop\-config \- read the desktop configuration and apply the accent color
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
get KEY
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
generate
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
apply
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
css
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
setup
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
enabled NAME
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
waybar
[TEMPLATE]
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
keys
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml for the shell scripts and writes the files that depend on the accent color.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-desktop\-config (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-desktop\-config); the process name is sway\-desktop\-config too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B get KEY
Print a value of the configuration; an unknown key exits 2.
.TP
.B generate
Write the files that depend on the color. It warns, on standard error, when the cursor the configuration asks for does
not take effect: a cursor_theme that is not installed (the automatic theme is used), or a seat ... xcursor_theme line
in a file of ~/.config/sway/config.d read after 00\-cursor.conf (50\-local.conf, for example) that sets another theme
or size and wins over cursor_theme and cursor_size. apply warns the same way.
.TP
.B apply
Write the files and reload Sway.
.TP
.B css
Print the accent colors as GTK CSS (@define\-color).
.TP
.B setup
Run by the packaged session on every login, before Sway starts: copy from the skeleton what is missing in the home
folder (a new ~/.config/sway/config.d/50-local.conf is written with its comments in the session's language),
update the system keyboard block in ~/.config/sway/config.d/50-local.conf while nobody has edited it, keep
~/.XCompose (' + c gives \[,c]) while the session uses the US international layout, then generate. The system keyboard
is whichever of /etc/default/keyboard, /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf and /etc/vconsole.conf changed last
(vconsole.conf with its XKB* keys; one with only KEYMAP counts only when the other two are missing).
On Debian and Ubuntu, localectl set\-x11\-keymap only writes /etc/vconsole.conf, which the boot rewrites from
/etc/default/keyboard: there, sudo dpkg\-reconfigure keyboard\-configuration is the change that lasts.
.TP
.B enabled NAME
Exit 0 if the component NAME is on in the [enabled] table of the configuration, 1 if it is off. NAME is a key of
[enabled], such as dock, or of [enabled.bar] with the bar. prefix, such as bar.weather. A key that is absent is
on; an unknown NAME prints a warning and counts as on. The session's sway\-if\-enabled helper uses it to skip the
components that are off.
.TP
.B waybar [TEMPLATE]
Write ~/.config/swaydesk\-desktop/waybar/config.jsonc: the Waybar configuration TEMPLATE (by default the
package's in the packaged session, ~/.config/waybar/config.jsonc otherwise) without the modules turned off in
[enabled.bar], and print its path. Without checkupdates (pacman\-contrib) in the PATH, or with
update_notifier = false in [enabled], the updates module is left out too: it is only for Arch, and without the
background check its count would go stale. The session's sway\-waybar runs it before each start and falls back to the
template when it fails. generate writes it too.
.TP
.B keys
Write only ~/.config/sway/config.d/00\-keys.conf, the includes of the shortcut profile (shortcuts in the
configuration), without the theme files. The session's Sway configuration runs it at every start and reload,
and reloads Sway when the file changed.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language (locale), accent color (accent), GTK and icon themes (gtk_theme, icon_theme), folder color (folder_color), file manager (file_manager), terminal (terminal: kitty unless set, for Ctrl+Alt+T and the terminal apps of the app grid), weather location (weather_location) and holidays (holidays). The fonts come from the GTK system font.
.IP
The [enabled] table turns session components off with false: dock, app_grid, switcher, notifications, osd,
clipboard_history, nightlight, bing_wallpaper, polkit_agent, update_notifier (on Arch, also the background check for
official, AUR, Flatpak and firmware updates, its notification and its bar icon; with it off, GNOME Software gets its
updates page back, which the Arch package turns off by default with allow\-updates=false, and "gsettings set
org.gnome.software allow\-updates true" does the same by hand), displays (the automatic
screen profiles and the rescue that turns the screens on when none is on; the Displays app stays). and autostart (the
XDG autostart apps of ~/.config/autostart and /etc/xdg/autostart, started through systemd; the entries that
duplicate what Swaydesk already runs, such as blueman, nm\-applet and the polkit agents, never start in its session). One key is off
unless set to true: input_method (fcitx5 as the session's input method, so dead keys and \(,c work in Chromium, Chrome,
Vivaldi and Electron apps, which ignore ~/.XCompose on Wayland; it needs the fcitx5 package, and writes
~/.config/fcitx5/config, ~/.config/fcitx5/profile from the session keyboard and the browsers' flag files only when they
are missing). The system file /etc/swaydesk/config.toml, which no package installs (the ISOs do), gives defaults for
the [enabled] table only: a key in the user's file wins. The [enabled.bar] table does
the same for the Waybar modules: weather, clock, media, recording, notifications, clipboard, language, system,
brightness, caffeine, bluetooth, network, volume, battery, power and updates (the Arch updates icon). A key that is absent is on. A change takes
effect at the next login; for the bar, also when Waybar restarts.
.IP
The shortcuts key picks the keyboard shortcut profile: swaydesk (the default), i3, hyprland, niri or dwm. generate
writes ~/.config/sway/config.d/00-keys.conf, which includes the keys of every profile (keys/base.conf) and then the
profile's own file (keys/<profile>.conf, in /usr/share/swaydesk\-desktop/sway/keys for the package session).
Run swaymsg reload after generate (keys, which the session runs, reloads by itself), or change the profile in the help window (Super+F1). The dwm profile uses Alt
as the modifier, as dwm does. The user's ~/.config/sway/config.d/50-local.conf is read after any profile and
wins over it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/00\-keys.conf
The includes of the shortcut profile, written by generate and keys.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk\-desktop/waybar/config.jsonc
The Waybar configuration without the modules turned off, written by waybar and generate.
.TP
.I /usr/share/swaydesk\-desktop/skel/
The skeleton that setup copies.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-theme (1)
